# dsh-desktop patch for tao

Vendored copy of `tao 0.35.3` (from the dsh CARGO_HOME registry) with one
local change, wired in via `[patch.crates-io]` in `../Cargo.toml`.

## Why

tao unconditionally installed a `GtkHeaderBar` (client-side titlebar) on every
Wayland window:

```rust
if is_wayland {
    WlHeader::setup(&window, &attributes.title);
}
```

That forced a GNOME-style header bar with a title and
minimize/maximize/close buttons on *every* compositor — including tiling
ones like driftwm, which already draw their own SSD chrome and want no client
titlebar. The `GTK_CSD=0` environment hint cannot help, because tao explicitly
calls `gtk_window_set_titlebar()` itself.

## The change

`src/platform_impl/linux/window.rs` — the forced header installation is
removed entirely (call site and the now-unused `WlHeader` import):

```rust
let window = window_builder.build();

// (no WlHeader::setup call — the compositor decides)
```

With no client titlebar, GTK3 negotiates `xdg-decoration` with the compositor,
so the *environment* decides:

- **driftwm** (SSD, `default_mode = "minimal"`, `GTK_CSD=0`) — border/shadow
  only, no titlebar. This is the desired behavior for the dsh desktop shell
  on a tiling WM.
- **GNOME / KDE** — the compositor serves a normal titlebar (or GTK draws its
  own CSD), so desktop users see a regular window.

X11/XWayland is unaffected — the code path was Wayland-only.

## How to refresh this copy

```sh
cp -r ~/.dsh/.cargo-home/registry/src/index.crates.io-*/tao-0.35.3 vendor/tao
# then remove the WlHeader::setup call + import, keep this README
```
